From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:56:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fix use-after-free of the rubber band when a MainWindow is
 destroyed

The window installs itself as an event filter on itself and on the find
panel. rubberBandManager is a member QObject whose parent is the window, so
its ~QObject, which runs after its QRubberBand member has been destroyed,
sends ChildRemoved to the window, and MainWindow::eventFilter() then calls
rubberBandManager.isVisible() on the destroyed rubber band (memcheck:
"Invalid read of size 1 ... RubberBandManager::isVisible() ... inside a block
free'd by ~RubberBandManager", closing the window with Ctrl+Q). The find
panel is deleted later still, by ~QWidget, with the same filter.

Sever both filters in ~MainWindow, as #7005 does for the docks.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 src/gui/MainWindow.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gui/MainWindow.cc b/src/gui/MainWindow.cc
index ed5dbf86f..131ecf061 100644
--- a/src/gui/MainWindow.cc
+++ b/src/gui/MainWindow.cc
@@ -629,6 +629,13 @@ MainWindow::~MainWindow()
     dock->disconnect(this);
     dock->removeEventFilter(this);
   }
+  // The window filters its own events and the find panel's too. rubberBandManager
+  // is a child QObject of this window, so its ~QObject, which runs after its own
+  // QRubberBand member is destroyed, sends ChildRemoved here, and eventFilter()
+  // would ask that destroyed rubber band whether it is visible; the find panel
+  // is deleted later still, by ~QWidget.
+  removeEventFilter(this);
+  find_panel->removeEventFilter(this);
 
   delete this->geometryWorker;
 }
